### Agent Orchestration Requirements

- Use tool calling with explicit permissions.
- Define strict input/output schemas.
- Avoid unnecessary agent-to-agent calls.
- Prevent infinite loops.
- Apply maximum tool-call limits.
- Track token consumption and provider costs.
- Support retries with idempotency.
- Log agent execution and errors.
- Use cheaper models for simple tasks.
- Escalate to more capable models only when necessary.

The system should support multiple AI providers rather than depending on one vendor.

Evaluate frameworks such as LangGraph, native tool-calling orchestration, or other suitable alternatives before choosing.

